            <div xml:id="d616">

                <pb facs="0552" n="542" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg542"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/9–2949: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Second Secretary of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bacon</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-09-29T15:00:00+08:00">September 29,
                            1949—3 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 29—5:30 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2190. Although CCP and PLA as such allotted only 18 seats on 89–man Presidium of
                    PCC, careful study of same list reveals at least 35 Presidium members are known
                    members CCP.</p>
                <p>Sent Department; repeated Peiping 375.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bacon</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
